#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""graphite-agent (Stage 2): a local assistant for Graphite OS.

Local inference only (llama.cpp `llama-server`, user service graphite-llm.service, 127.0.0.1).
A user-session daemon (graphite-agent.socket/.service, a 0600 Unix socket in XDG_RUNTIME_DIR,
peer-UID checked) runs one answer at a time as a persisted task: running -> done / failed /
cancelled / interrupted (a task cut off by a crash is marked interrupted, never replayed). Every
tool call is validated here, outside the model; the tools are read-only and bounded (time, call
count, output size). Notes ("memory") are saved only when the user asks, kept in SQLite FTS5 on
this computer, and can be listed, forgotten and exported. No shell, no writes, no cloud.

  graphite-agent ask [--jsonl] QUESTION   answer one question (panel uses --jsonl)
  graphite-agent toggle|open|close        the panel (qs -c graphite-agent), Super+Shift+A
  graphite-agent cancel                   stop any answer in progress
  graphite-agent unload                   cancel + stop the model service (frees its RAM)
  graphite-agent status [--json]          model file / service / server / daemon state
  graphite-agent remember TEXT            save a note the assistant may use in answers
  graphite-agent notes [--json]           list saved notes
  graphite-agent forget ID|--all          delete a note (or all notes) for good
  graphite-agent export [FILE]            write notes + history as JSON (default: stdout)
  graphite-agent history [--json] [N]     recent questions; history clear|on|off
  graphite-agent audit [TASK] [--json]    tool calls and state changes of recent tasks
  graphite-agent setup-model              repair/fallback: verify the model, else put a copy in
                                          ~/.local/share/graphite-agent/models (from a local
                                          graphite-agent-model package, else download, sha256)
  graphite-agent serve [ARGS]             exec llama-server (graphite-llm.service runs this)
  graphite-agent daemon                   the session daemon (graphite-agent.service runs this)

The model normally comes from the graphite-agent-model package (/usr/share/graphite-agent/models).
"""
